            <zone h='35333' id='17' name='Our forecast cuts the average error by more than half' w='56000' x='571' y='63778'>
              <layout-cache minwidth='260' type-h='fixed' type-w='scalable' />
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone forceUpdate='true' h='35333' id='18' type-v2='text' w='42858' x='56571' y='63778'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>What this means:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>1. Smoking combined with obesity drive costs: Obese smokers are 11% of members but 34% of claim costs. Our regression showed obesity raises costs mainly for smokers, a pattern that only appears when the two are analyzed together.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>2. The forecast is reliable for budgeting. Tested on members it never saw, our model cuts the average error by more than half ($3,700 vs. $8,200 per member).</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>3. Recommendation: Focus prevention programs (quit-smoking, weight management) on smokers with obesity, where the savings per member are largest, and collect fuller health history to explain the few high-cost members our data can&apos;t.</run>
              </formatted-text>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
